From: Tezuka firmware
Subject: [PATCH] net: macb: allow jumbo frames on Zynq-7000

Streaming IQ over the board's gigabit link tops out around 480-560
Mbit/s, and that ceiling is a per-packet CPU wall, not bandwidth: during
a saturating transfer both Cortex-A9 cores sit at 0% idle with roughly
63% system and 33% softirq time. At MTU 1500 with no TSO on this
controller, 57 MiB/s is about 40k transmitted segments per second, each
one built and completed in software. Fewer, larger frames is the only
lever that meaningfully reduces that cost.

zynq_config does not set MACB_CAPS_JUMBO, so macb_change_mtu() refuses
any MTU above 1500:

  # ip link set eth0 mtu 4000
  RTNETLINK answers: Invalid argument

The zynqmp_config immediately below it does set the flag together with
.jumbo_max_len, and the Zynq-7000 GEM has the same Jumbo Max Length
register that macb_init() programs via gem_writel(bp, JML, ...). Set
both here in the same way.

This changes nothing on its own: the interface still comes up at MTU
1500, and the capability only permits a larger MTU to be configured. On
this firmware the rootfs is a RAM disk and the MTU is not persisted, so
a reboot returns the board to 1500 regardless.

Caveat worth recording: the Zynq-7000 GEM's TX packet buffer is 4 KB, so
a full 9000 byte frame may not be storable and forwardable even though
the JML register accepts 10240. The usable MTU is expected to be nearer
4000, which is still about 2.6x fewer packets. Raise the MTU
incrementally and verify, and remember every hop plus the peer has to
agree or traffic silently blackholes.

Signed-off-by: Tezuka firmware
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c	2026-09-05 12:30:43
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c	2026-09-05 12:30:43
@@ -4960,10 +4960,11 @@
 
 static const struct macb_config zynq_config = {
 	.caps = MACB_CAPS_GIGABIT_MODE_AVAILABLE | MACB_CAPS_NO_GIGABIT_HALF |
-		MACB_CAPS_NEEDS_RSTONUBR,
+		MACB_CAPS_NEEDS_RSTONUBR | MACB_CAPS_JUMBO,
 	.dma_burst_length = 16,
 	.clk_init = macb_clk_init,
 	.init = macb_init,
+	.jumbo_max_len = 10240,
 	.usrio = &macb_default_usrio,
 };
 
